TITLE:: FxRackBranch
summary:: one chain of a rack: its effects, level, mute, solo and place in the line-up
categories:: Libraries>ParaEQ
related:: Classes/FxRack, Classes/FxChain

DESCRIPTION::
One of the chains an link::Classes/FxRack:: runs side by side. Made by
link::Classes/FxRack#-addBranch::, never by hand.

code::
(
r = FxRack();
b = r.addBranch("dry");
b.level = -6;
b.chain.add(ParaEQ());
r.branches.collect(_.name);
);
::

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: rack
The link::Classes/FxRack:: it belongs to.

METHOD:: chain
Its effects: an owned link::Classes/FxChain::. Add to it, take out of it and
reorder it as any chain; the rack places its group and rebuilds it.

METHOD:: name
What the chain is called.

METHOD:: level
In dB, -60 to +6. -60 is silence. Default 0.

METHOD:: mute
Set true to silence the chain.

METHOD:: solo
Set true and only the soloed chains of the rack are heard.

METHOD:: align
Whether the chain takes part in the line-up. Off, it is not held back and the
others do not wait for it. Default true.

METHOD:: latency
How late the chain is by itself, in seconds: the latencies of the effects that
are on in it, added up.

METHOD:: heldBack
How long the rack holds the chain back so the others catch up, in seconds.

METHOD:: delay
The same in samples.

METHOD:: summary
What the chain is made of, as a line: "compressor → eq", or "-" when empty.

METHOD:: index
Its place among the rack's chains.
